112
00:11:49.000 --> 00:12:03.824
<v Maya>Right. And for the original abstracts, people used causal language 71.3% of the time. But for the rewritten, perfectly cautious, totally scrubbed versions, the readers still injected causal language 49.6% of the</v>

113
00:12:03.844 --> 00:12:04.084
<v Maya>time.</v>

114
00:12:04.304 --> 00:12:05.305
<v Daniel>Almost half the time.</v>

115
00:12:05.425 --> 00:12:10.106
<v Maya>Half the time, the reader read a careful paper and summarized it with a causal claim that wasn't even there.</v>

116
00:12:10.346 --> 00:12:16.620
<v Daniel>And this is where we bring in Samuel Gershman and Tomer Ullman's 2023 background paper on causal implicatures.</v>

117
00:12:17.212 --> 00:12:19.294
<v Maya>Oh, this paper is so important for this.</v>

118
00:12:19.414 --> 00:12:31.722
<v Daniel>It really is. They proved experimentally that humans naturally infer causation from correlational statements. Even if you just write, X is associated with an increased risk of Y, people read that as X causes Y.</v>

119
00:12:31.843 --> 00:12:40.729
<v Maya>You know what's crazy about this? It makes me wonder if we literally can't help it. Like, if I read two facts side by side, my brain instantly tries to connect them with a because.</v>

120
00:12:41.089 --> 00:12:44.050
<v Daniel>Are we just biologically hardwired to reject coincidence?</v>

121
00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:53.435
<v Maya>Maybe, because a purely statistical association doesn't give us a tool to survive or act on the world, but a cause-and-effect relationship does.</v>

122
00:12:53.575 --> 00:13:01.118
<v Daniel>We are narrative creatures. Our cognitive default is to see causal models of the world, and this is the tension the scientists are exploiting.</v>

123
00:13:01.383 --> 00:13:11.308
<v Maya>Okay, but let's follow the logic here. If humans are fundamentally flawed readers who inject causation because we want a story, what happens when we outsource the reading to a machine?</v>

124
00:13:11.828 --> 00:13:12.208
<v Daniel>Ah, yes.</v>

125
00:13:12.428 --> 00:13:23.904
